[{:db/id 17592186162057 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6da9aedf-d051-5c8d-9ea5-b796001b82b1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162264 :question/problem "If $\\text{Var}[X]=8,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[2X].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158786 :answer-field/correct 17592186158787 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162058 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2adf151d-6d7b-5aee-975a-4588dddc072c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162267 :question/problem "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=7,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[2-5X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-5$ and $b=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2-5X] & =(-5)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=7.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6)+{9}^{2}\\cdot f(9) \\\\  & =25(\\frac{1}{5})+36(\\frac{2}{5})+81(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{259}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{259}{5}-{7}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{259}{5}-49 \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2-5X] & =25\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{14}{5} \\\\  & =14\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158804 :answer-field/correct 17592186158808 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-6da9aedf-d051-5c8d-9ea5-b796001b82b1" :question/id #uuid "6da9aedf-d051-5c8d-9ea5-b796001b82b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-109056" :question/problem "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=2,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\sqrt{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X] & ={\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=2.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+16\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X] & =3\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ef907e56-83d3-5832-9059-ba2b6e97be1a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ef907e56-83d3-5832-9059-ba2b6e97be1a" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef907e56-83d3-5832-9059-ba2b6e97be1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2a01301e-2613-5381-a06c-9e16aa051fd8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1ffc334f-bda6-5020-8972-7c141e811580" "answer-bea01d67-a086-5031-9b05-53086e759f6a" "answer-2a01301e-2613-5381-a06c-9e16aa051fd8" "answer-559bb6ee-9e3b-59fc-b4ec-1934f445e465" "answer-3e1bb640-287c-5a4d-9809-a95f12e541cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ffc334f-bda6-5020-8972-7c141e811580" :answer/id #uuid "1ffc334f-bda6-5020-8972-7c141e811580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bea01d67-a086-5031-9b05-53086e759f6a" :answer/id #uuid "bea01d67-a086-5031-9b05-53086e759f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a01301e-2613-5381-a06c-9e16aa051fd8" :answer/id #uuid "2a01301e-2613-5381-a06c-9e16aa051fd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-559bb6ee-9e3b-59fc-b4ec-1934f445e465" :answer/id #uuid "559bb6ee-9e3b-59fc-b4ec-1934f445e465" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e1bb640-287c-5a4d-9809-a95f12e541cd" :answer/id #uuid "3e1bb640-287c-5a4d-9809-a95f12e541cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2adf151d-6d7b-5aee-975a-4588dddc072c" :question/id #uuid "2adf151d-6d7b-5aee-975a-4588dddc072c" :question/math-academy-id "q-109086" :question/problem "If $\\text{Var}[X]=18,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X+1].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $b=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X+1] & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9be7f666-e571-52b8-923e-291edd79be24"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9be7f666-e571-52b8-923e-291edd79be24" :answer-field/id #uuid "9be7f666-e571-52b8-923e-291edd79be24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e9447cf-647a-5fa5-b1b7-8ad767262b04" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a7e38c85-b6da-52ad-a873-fe8715cae083" "answer-0e9447cf-647a-5fa5-b1b7-8ad767262b04" "answer-84d7e9cc-2b46-5e49-827d-3dc43ec7a3fa" "answer-a04fede6-c5e8-5346-92ee-0dfe50e7363c" "answer-26c878c9-4005-5ffb-b62a-ccf12e7653a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7e38c85-b6da-52ad-a873-fe8715cae083" :answer/id #uuid "a7e38c85-b6da-52ad-a873-fe8715cae083" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e9447cf-647a-5fa5-b1b7-8ad767262b04" :answer/id #uuid "0e9447cf-647a-5fa5-b1b7-8ad767262b04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84d7e9cc-2b46-5e49-827d-3dc43ec7a3fa" :answer/id #uuid "84d7e9cc-2b46-5e49-827d-3dc43ec7a3fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a04fede6-c5e8-5346-92ee-0dfe50e7363c" :answer/id #uuid "a04fede6-c5e8-5346-92ee-0dfe50e7363c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26c878c9-4005-5ffb-b62a-ccf12e76